{
  "_comment": "Seed crawl list. `v0` is the starter index — crawl these first. `backlog` is held for later, each with the reason it didn't make v0. `platform_guess` is a hint; the ingestion worker detects the real one. Domains need a verification pass before the first crawl.",
  "_fabric_gate": {
    "why": "'Good fabrics' is the criterion that separates a taste index from a catalog, and unlike aesthetic judgment it is machine-checkable — fiber composition sits in the Shopify payload or product copy for most brands.",
    "how": "During ingestion, parse fiber composition per item and compute a natural-fiber ratio (cotton, linen, wool, cashmere, silk, hemp, leather, TENCEL/lyocell). Roll up to a brand-level median.",
    "gate": "Brands whose median natural-fiber ratio falls below ~50% get flagged for review before entering the index, regardless of how fashionable they look.",
    "note": "This turns a taste criterion into an automated index gate, and feeds the Boutique Score in Feature 3 — cheap synthetics correlate hard with the chains we want to rank down. It should also be run against the v0 list itself as a check on these hand-picks."
  },
  "_price_gate": {
    "target": "Under $100 average preferred (tier A). $100–300 acceptable (tier B). No floor — cheaper is fine.",
    "method": "Average of all variant prices per product, averaged across the catalog. First-page sample (250 products) is sufficient; full pagination is not required.",
    "exclusions": "Non-apparel product types (home, furniture, decor, candles, apothecary/beauty, books, pet) and junk SKUs (gift cards, shipping protection, swatches, samples) dropped before pricing.",
    "currency": "Detected via /meta.json, converted at approximate rates (EUR 1.08, GBP 1.27, SEK 0.095, DKK 0.145). Indicative, not live.",
    "measured_on": "2026-08-15"
  },
